# ── KEY MATERIAL. Never committed, never in .env, never read at runtime. ───────
# Anything key-shaped stays out of the repo on principle, regardless of what it
# currently controls. It is deliberately NOT in .env either, because .env is
# loaded by the app and mirrored into Netlify env — a key that no running code
# path can reach cannot be leaked by one. The patterns are broad so a future key
# file cannot miss the net by being named slightly differently.
#
# ⚠️ CORRECTED 2026-07-24. This block used to claim the cold owner EOA in .keys/
# was "the root of trust for the agent registry: whoever holds it OWNS the
# agents." THAT WAS NEVER TRUE. The cold owner 0xc85b3d9BdEb… has never owned any
# agent identity on-chain. The ERC-8004 identities are owned by the agent's Circle
# DEVELOPER-CONTROLLED SCA at 0xc54d47211997aca90ef4fcfbc742a3b511b4e621 — the
# same custodial account class that holds the agent float. Confirmed on-chain:
# ownerOf(850337) == 0xc54D47211997aCA90Ef4fCfBc742a3b511B4e621.
#
# The same false claim was removed from agent-metadata/*.json when the ownership
# model was stated plainly; this copy was missed because it lives in a comment.
# Holding .keys/cold-owner.json grants NO authority over the agent identities.
# The patterns below stay anyway — key hygiene does not depend on the key
# mattering.
.keys/
*.key
*.privkey
cold-owner*.json

# ── Incidental run output from scripts/register-identity.mjs ───────────────────
# Raw dump of this wallet's NFT holdings, written as audit evidence for the
# existence check. Not credentials — just noise that shouldn't be committed
# carelessly.
# NOTE the deliberate asymmetry: agent-metadata/REGISTERED-IDENTITY.json is NOT
# ignored. The agentId is public, persisting it is the entire point of that
# script, and committing it is a durable copy of the value whose loss caused the
# orphan-wallet excavation in the first place.
# ⚠️ BROADENED 2026-07-31 — the exact-path form ALREADY FAILED ONCE. A second dump written
# as `.nft-enumeration-dd-service.json` did not match `.nft-enumeration.json` and sat
# untracked-but-unignored, one `git add .` from being committed. That is precisely the miss
# the broad `.keys/` and `*.key` patterns above exist to prevent, so this pattern is broad
# for the same reason: a future dump must not escape by being named slightly differently.
agent-metadata/.nft-enumeration*.json

# Money-path run records from scripts/fire-ub-spend.mjs — hold a live transferId/txHash.
# Durable ON DISK by design (evidence must survive a timeout), but never committed.
ub-spend-capture-*.json

# x402 seller census: scratch scan output is ignored; PUBLISHED artifacts are not.
#
# ⛔ THIS RULE ONCE CAUSED A CLAIM TO BECOME UNRECOVERABLE. It withheld the per-address rows
# on editorial grounds ("the distribution is the finding; who occupies which position in it
# is not"), and the old comment here claimed seller-census.mjs "reproduces the full
# per-address data locally in ~5 minutes". THE SCAN reproduces — the INDEX HARVEST does not:
# the discovery index is live and its Base listing count moved 836 -> 845 within two hours on
# 2026-08-27. So a claim derived from the rows (the rail table's "19 vanilla-declaring
# addresses, 18 (95%) show receipts") could not be checked once the index moved, and had to
# be WITHDRAWN rather than corrected. See docs/x402-seller-census-2026-08-25.md.
#
# ⭐ THE RULE NOW: if a published document derives a claim from these rows, the rows ship with
# it — including the classifier INPUT verbatim, not just a derived label. Add a negation here
# for any such artifact rather than relying on someone remembering to force-add it.
# ⭐⭐ RULE INVERTED 2026-08-27. It previously ignored `scripts/x402-census/census-*.json` by
# default and carved out a negation PER ARTIFACT. That is unsafe by default: a new artifact is
# swallowed silently unless someone remembers to allowlist it, and "someone remembers" is the
# exact property that made the failure above possible. It very nearly repeated the same day —
# census-2026-08-25.per-address.json did not stage, and was caught only by reading git status.
# NOW: only the named scratch outputs are ignored. Anything else written into that directory is
# TRACKED BY DEFAULT. A new harvest or rows file needs no gitignore edit to survive.
# ⚠️ These three names are the scripts' hardcoded working files — they are run output, not
# evidence, and each is rewritten in place on every run.
census-out.json
payto-catalogue-out.json
catalogue-effect-out.json
scripts/x402-census/census-out.json
scripts/x402-census/payto-catalogue-out.json
scripts/x402-census/catalogue-effect-out.json
